// P3I.7 / SM16.1–SM16.6, exercise E3 (`ex3-drawings/goal.png`, step-04–06; lesson
// `16-drawings`) on a Sheet Metal Box stand-in: a 200 × 125 × 150 block converted with its four
// bottom edges bent and the top left open (1.5 mm sheet, R1.5 bends).
// 01 The part studio with the box; 02 Parts list → right-click: Create Drawing of Sheet Metal
//    Box… and Create drawing of flat pattern…; 03 Create Drawing: ANSI_A_MM.dwt, Four views;
// 04 the four folded views; 05 dimensioned (width and height of the front view);
// 06 Insert sheet → Insert view → Flat patterns filter; 07 the flat picked, following the
//    cursor; 08 placed: outline, bend lines, bend notes "DOWN 90.0° R1.5" along each line;
// 09 a bend note dragged off its line (leader); 10 another dropped back near its line;
// 11 the flat dimensioned (overall width, a bend line to the edge); 12 right-click → Hide bend
//    notes; 13 undo shows them again.
Scenario(
    start: Some("document"),
    steps: [
        WaitFor("document-shell"),
        Wait(30),
        Custom("flat-drawing box"),
        Wait(90),
        Key("F"),
        Wait(30),
        MoveTo(1500, 960),
        Wait(3),
        Screenshot("01-sheet-metal-box"),
        RightClick(ui("part-row-sheet-metal-box")),
        Wait(6),
        Hover(ui("part-drawing")),
        Wait(4),
        Screenshot("02-parts-list-menu"),
        Click(ui("part-drawing")),
        WaitFor("create-drawing-dialog"),
        Wait(8),
        Click(ui("template-row-ANSI_A_MM.dwt")),
        Wait(5),
        Click(ui("template-option-four-views")),
        Wait(8),
